      "hints": [
        "Factor out $4$ to get $4(x^2 + 5x) + 6$.",
        "Complete the square for $x^2 + 5x$ as $(x + \\frac{5}{2})^2 - \\frac{25}{4}$.",
        "Expand and simplify constants."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Factor out $4$ from the quadratic and linear terms:\n$$4x^2 + 20x + 6 = 4\\left(x^2 + 5x\\right) + 6$$",
        "Complete the square for $x^2 + 5x$:\n$$= 4\\left(\\left(x + \\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2 - \\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2\\right) + 6 = 4\\left(x + \\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2 - 4\\left(\\frac{25}{4}\\right) + 6$$",
        "Simplify the constant term:\n$$= 4\\left(x + \\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2 - 25 + 6 = 4\\left(x + \\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2 - 19$$"
      ],
